==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ruffle.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*: {{rhymes|ʌfəl}}

===Noun===
'''ruffle'''

# Any [[gathered]] or [[curled]] strip of fabric added as [[trim]] or [[decoration]].
#: ''She loved the dress with the lace '''ruffle''' at the hem.

====Translations====
{{trans-top|strip of fabric}}
* Finnish: {{t|fi|röyhelö}}
{{trans-mid}}
* German: {{t-|de|Rüsche|f}}
* Spanish: {{t|es|volante|m}}
{{trans-bottom}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|ruffl|ing}}

# {{transitive}} To make a [[ruffle]] in; to curl or [[flute]], ''as'' an edge of fabric.
#: ''Ruffle the end of the cuff.''
# {{transitive}} To [[disturb]]; especially, to cause to [[flutter]].
#: ''The wind '''ruffled''' the papers.''

